      "body": "**Actionable comments posted: 8**\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>.gitignore (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `1-31`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n> \n> **`.gitignore`에 `dist` 디렉토리를 추가하세요.**\n> \n> `dist/` 디렉토리의 파일들이 현재 git으로 추적되고 있습니다. Vite의 빌드 출력 디렉토리를 저장소에 커밋하면 저장소 크기가 증가하고 불필요한 병합 충돌을 야기할 수 있습니다. Vercel과 GitHub Actions 모두 배포 시점에 자동으로 빌드하므로, `.gitignore`에 `dist/`를 추가하고 빌드 결과물은 배포 파이프라인에서만 생성되도록 해야 합니다.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In @.gitignore around lines 1 - 31, Add the Vite build output directory \"dist/\"\n> to .gitignore so the repository stops tracking build artifacts; open the\n> existing .gitignore (which already lists \"dist-ssr\") and add a new line with\n> \"dist/\" (or \"dist\") to ensure the dist directory is ignored by git and no longer\n> committed.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (6)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>src/common/types/CardInfoType.ts (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`2-10`: **`cardNumbers`를 4개 고정 길이 타입으로 좁혀보세요.**\n\n`cardNumbers: string[]`는 현재 3·5 또는 임의 길이 배열도 타입상 허용합니다. 하지만 코드 전반에서 4개 그룹으로 고정되어 있습니다:\n- `CardRegisterPage`: `useState(['', '', '', ''])` (정확히 4개)\n- `NumberField`: `INPUT_COUNT = 4` 상수 정의  \n- 모든 컴포넌트: `.map()` 사용 시 인덱스 0-3만 참조\n\n타입을 `[string, string, string, string]` 또는 브랜드 타입으로 정의하면, 잘못된 길이의 배열을 넘기려는 실수를 컴파일 타임에 차단할 수 있습니다. 현재 호출부를 먼저 훑어본 후, 고정 길이 타입 정의 → setter 서명 수정 순서로 진행하는 것을 추천합니다.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/common/types/CardInfoType.ts` around lines 2 - 10, The cardNumbers field\nis declared too loosely as string[]; change it to a fixed 4-tuple (e.g. [string,\nstring, string, string] or a branded alias) and update the setter signature in\nCardInfoHandlersType (setCardNumbers) to accept that same tuple type so callers\nlike CardRegisterPage (useState(['','','',''])) and components relying on\nNumberField/INPUT_COUNT=4 get compile-time safety; first scan call sites that\npass arrays and adjust them to return/accept the 4-tuple type, then update the\nCardInfoType.cardNumbers and CardInfoHandlersType.setCardNumbers types\naccordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.storybook/preview.ts (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`12-17`: **a11y 검사 강도를 언제 CI 차단 모드로 올릴지 기준을 정해두면 좋겠습니다.**\n\nLine 16의 `test: 'todo'`는 현재 스토리북 UI에서만 경고를 표시하고, 실제 Vitest CLI/CI 실행 시에는 a11y 검사를 스킵합니다. CI에서 강제로 접근성 위반을 차단하려면 `test: 'error'`로 변경해야 합니다.\n\n진행 전략으로는 `'error'`로 설정한 후, 초기에 많은 위반이 발견되면 일부 스토리에 한해 `'todo'`로 표시하여 추적한 뒤, 순차적으로 수정하여 제거하는 방식을 추천합니다. 이러한 단계적 전환의 시점(예: 핵심 컴포넌트 스토리 완료 시점)을 팀 규칙으로 미리 정하면 효과적입니다.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.storybook/preview.ts around lines 12 - 17, The current a11y config uses\ntest: 'todo' (the line setting test: 'todo') which only shows violations in the\nStorybook UI; change this to test: 'error' to make Vitest/CI fail on\naccessibility violations, and if initial failures are numerous, mark specific\nstory-level a11y settings as 'todo' while you iteratively fix them—apply the\nchange to the a11y config where the test property is defined and document a\nrollout rule (e.g., switch to 'error' for core components first, keep\nnon‑critical stories as 'todo' temporarily).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/feature/CardRegister/components/CardPreviewSection/CardBrandLogo/CardBrandLogo.tsx (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-2`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**public 이미지 참조는 깊은 상대경로 import보다 루트 절대경로가 안전합니다.**\n\nLine 1, Line 2 방식은 파일 이동 시 쉽게 깨지고 경로 가독성이 낮습니다. Vite에서는 public 자산을 `/images/...`처럼 참조하는 쪽이 더 단순합니다.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>리팩터 예시</summary>\n\n```diff\n-import visaImg from '../../../../../../public/images/Visa.png';\n-import masterCardImg from '../../../../../../public/images/Mastercard.png';\n import styled from 'styled-components';\n@@\n-  return (\n-    <BrandLogoImg\n-      src={brandName === 'visa' ? visaImg : masterCardImg}\n-      alt={brandName === 'visa' ? 'Visa' : 'MasterCard'}\n-    />\n-  );\n+  return (\n+    <BrandLogoImg\n+      src={brandName === 'visa' ? '/images/Visa.png' : '/images/Mastercard.png'}\n+      alt={brandName === 'visa' ? 'Visa' : 'MasterCard'}\n+    />\n+  );\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn\n`@src/feature/CardRegister/components/CardPreviewSection/CardBrandLogo/CardBrandLogo.tsx`\naround lines 1 - 2, 현재 CardBrandLogo.tsx에서 visaImg와 masterCardImg를 깊은 상대경로로\nimport하고 있어 파일 이동 시 깨질 위험이 있습니다; CardBrandLogo.tsx의 import visaImg와 import\nmasterCardImg를 public 폴더의 루트 절대경로 방식으로 바꿔 (/images/Visa.png,\n/images/Mastercard.png 같이) 참조하도록 수정하고, 컴포넌트 내에서 해당 변수명(visaImg, masterCardImg)을\n그대로 사용하도록 유지하세요.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/styles/reset.css (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`11-24`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**리셋 파일에 레이아웃 책임이 섞여 있습니다.**\n\nLine 11~24의 viewport 높이/센터링은 리셋보다는 페이지 컨테이너 책임에 가깝습니다. 전역 리셋에 두면 다른 화면/스토리북 렌더링에 의도치 않은 영향을 줄 수 있습니다.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>분리 예시</summary>\n\n```diff\n html,\n body,\n `#root` {\n   min-height: 100%;\n-  height: 100vh;\n }\n \n body {\n-  display: flex;\n-  justify-content: center;\n-  align-items: center;\n   line-height: 1.5;\n   -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;\n }\n```\n</details>\n\n레이아웃 정렬은 `CardRegisterPage` 래퍼(또는 App 루트 컨테이너)로 이동하는 것을 권장합니다.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/styles/reset.css` around lines 11 - 24, The reset.css currently mixes\nlayout responsibilities into global selectors (html, body, `#root`) by setting\nheight:100vh and centering via flexbox; remove the viewport-height and centering\nrules from these selectors so the reset only contains neutral defaults, and move\nlayout/centering styles into the page-level wrapper (e.g., CardRegisterPage\nwrapper component or the App root container) by applying the flexbox centering\nand min-height/height rules there instead; update selectors referencing html,\nbody, `#root` in reset.css to omit display, justify-content, align-items,\nmin-height and height so Storybook and other pages aren’t affected.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/feature/CardRegister/components/CardPreviewSection/CardPreviewSection.stories.tsx (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`23-31`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**브랜드 분기 검증을 위해 MasterCard 스토리도 추가하면 좋겠습니다.**\n\n현재 Filled는 Visa 케이스만 확인됩니다. Storybook 시각 회귀 관점에서 MasterCard 케이스를 별도 스토리로 두면 로고/프리뷰 검증이 더 명확해집니다.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>추가 예시</summary>\n\n```diff\n export const Filled: Story = {\n   args: {\n     cardInfo: {\n       cardNumbers: ['4123', '5678', '1234', '5678'],\n       expiryMonth: '12',\n       expiryYear: '30',\n     },\n   },\n };\n+\n+export const MasterCardFilled: Story = {\n+  args: {\n+    cardInfo: {\n+      cardNumbers: ['5123', '5678', '1234', '5678'],\n+      expiryMonth: '09',\n+      expiryYear: '28',\n+    },\n+  },\n+};\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn\n`@src/feature/CardRegister/components/CardPreviewSection/CardPreviewSection.stories.tsx`\naround lines 23 - 31, Add a separate Storybook story for a MasterCard case in\nthe same file alongside the existing export const Filled: Story to enable\nbrand-specific visual regression checks; create a new export (e.g., export const\nMasterCard: Story) that mirrors Filled but sets cardInfo.cardNumbers to a\nMasterCard BIN prefix (e.g., starting with \"51\" or \"55\") and the same\nexpiryMonth/expiryYear fields so the preview renders the MasterCard logo/preview\nfor testing.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/feature/CardRegister/components/InfoInputSection/InfoInputSection.tsx (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`22-24`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**렌더 단계의 `console.log`는 제거하거나 `useEffect`로 분리해 주세요.**\n\nLine 22~24는 렌더마다 실행되어 디버그 노이즈를 만들고(특히 StrictMode) 유지보수성을 떨어뜨립니다.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/feature/CardRegister/components/InfoInputSection/InfoInputSection.tsx`\naround lines 22 - 24, The render currently contains a console.log('error')\ninside the InfoInputSection component that runs on every render when isError is\ntrue; remove this inline log or move it into a useEffect to avoid render-time\nside effects (e.g., add useEffect(() => { if (isError) { /* log */ } },\n[isError]) ), referencing the isError check in InfoInputSection to locate and\nreplace the console.log.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn @.github/pull_request_template.md:\n- Around line 28-31: The PR template currently has checklist items pre-checked\nand a hardcoded deployment URL; update .github/pull_request_template.md to\nrestore template defaults by changing the three checked items (\"[x] 기능 요구\n사항...\", \"[x] 기본적인 프로그래밍 요구 사항...\", \"[x] 배포한 데모 페이지에 정상적으로 접근할 수 있나요?\") to\nunchecked boxes (\"[ ]\") and replace the specific URL\n\"https://react-payments-sage.vercel.app/\" with a placeholder instruction like\n\"<배포 링크 입력>\" or \"배포 링크: (여기에 입력)\" so future PRs start with an empty checklist\nand a placeholder deployment link.\n\nIn `@package.json`:\n- Around line 15-43: package.json currently pins \"typescript\": \"~6.0.2\" and\n\"typescript-eslint\": \"^8.58.2\", which is out of range for typescript-eslint\n(requires <6.1.0 and may not officially support TS 6.x); fix by either upgrading\nthe typescript-eslint package to a version that adds TypeScript 6 support (bump\n\"@typescript-eslint/*\" / \"typescript-eslint\" to v8.59.0+ or the specific\nworkspace package that provides that support) or by downgrading \"typescript\" to\na supported 5.x release (e.g., ^5.x) so it falls within typescript-eslint's\nsupported range; update the package.json entries for \"typescript\" and/or\n\"typescript-eslint\" accordingly and run npm/yarn install and the project's\nlint/type checks to verify no further peer conflicts.\n\nIn `@README.md`:\n- Line 121: The fenced code block that shows the src/ directory tree is missing\na language identifier (causing MD040 lint); update the fenced block that\ncontains \"src/ ├── common/ ... └── main.tsx\" by adding a language tag (e.g.,\n```text or ```bash) immediately after the opening backticks so the markdown\nlinter recognizes the code block.\n\nIn `@src/common/components/Input/Input.tsx`:\n- Around line 24-29: The input styled component in Input.tsx currently removes\noutlines and uses the same border color for error focus (see &:focus and\nprops.$strokeMode), making keyboard focus hard to see; restore accessible\nkeyboard focus by adding a :focus-visible rule that adds a visible focus ring\n(e.g., box-shadow or outline) that differs from the error border color, using\nSTROKE_MODE_COLOR.error and FOCUS_COLOR to decide styling based on\nprops.$strokeMode so error state keeps its error border but still shows a clear\nfocus indicator when focused via keyboard.\n\nIn `@src/common/components/Label/Label.tsx`:\n- Around line 3-11: The Label component (StyledLabel and Label) is not accepting\nhtmlFor so it cannot be associated with an input; update Label to accept props\nlike htmlFor?: string and other passthrough props (e.g., children/value and rest\nprops) and forward htmlFor to StyledLabel so callers can connect the label to an\ninput, or if the intention is purely presentational, replace StyledLabel usage\nwith a non-semantic span; modify the Label function signature to accept and\npass-through htmlFor (and any other HTMLLabelElement attributes) to StyledLabel\nto restore accessibility.\n\nIn\n`@src/feature/CardRegister/components/CardPreviewSection/CardBrandLogo/CardBrandLogo.tsx`:\n- Line 10: The BrandLogoImg rendered in the CardBrandLogo component currently\nlacks an alt attribute; update the JSX in CardBrandLogo (where BrandLogoImg is\nreturned) to include a descriptive alt prop that reflects the brand (e.g.,\nalt={brandName === 'visa' ? 'Visa logo' : 'Mastercard logo'}) so screen readers\ncan announce the card brand; ensure the alt text is concise and uses the\nexisting brandName conditional logic.\n\nIn\n`@src/feature/CardRegister/components/CardPreviewSection/CardPreviewContainer/CardPreviewContainer.tsx`:\n- Around line 11-16: The brand detection runs even when the 16-digit number is\nincomplete because fullNumber is padded with '#' and checks like\nfullNumber.startsWith('4') run early; update the logic in CardPreviewContainer\n(use the fullNumber and cardNumbers variables) to first verify the card is\ncomplete (e.g., ensure fullNumber does not contain '#' or all cardNumbers chunks\nare length 4) and only then perform brand checks (the Visa startsWith('4') and\nthe masterCard prefix Number(fullNumber.slice(0,2)) between 51–55); if\nincomplete, skip returning a brand so the logo doesn't show prematurely.\n\nIn `@src/feature/CardRegister/components/InfoInputSection/InfoInputSection.tsx`:\n- Around line 17-42: The current single boolean isError gets overwritten by\nindependent child calls (NumberField, ExpiryField, CvcField) so one field can\nclear another's error; replace it with a per-field aggregated error state (e.g.,\nconst [fieldErrors, setFieldErrors] = useState({number:false, expiry:false,\ncvc:false}) and derive const isError =\nObject.values(fieldErrors).some(Boolean)). Update the props you pass into\nNumberField, ExpiryField, and CvcField to accept a field-specific setter (or a\ngeneric setFieldError(fieldName, bool) function) instead of setIsError, and\nchange any references to setIsError to call setFieldErrors or\nsetFieldError('number'|'expiry'|'cvc', value) so each component updates only its\nown key while the parent computes the combined isError.\n\n---\n\nOutside diff comments:\nIn @.gitignore:\n- Around line 1-31: Add the Vite build output directory \"dist/\" to .gitignore so\nthe repository stops tracking build artifacts; open the existing .gitignore\n(which already lists \"dist-ssr\") and add a new line with \"dist/\" (or \"dist\") to\nensure the dist directory is ignored by git and no longer committed.\n\n---\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn @.storybook/preview.ts:\n- Around line 12-17: The current a11y config uses test: 'todo' (the line setting\ntest: 'todo') which only shows violations in the Storybook UI; change this to\ntest: 'error' to make Vitest/CI fail on accessibility violations, and if initial\nfailures are numerous, mark specific story-level a11y settings as 'todo' while\nyou iteratively fix them—apply the change to the a11y config where the test\nproperty is defined and document a rollout rule (e.g., switch to 'error' for\ncore components first, keep non‑critical stories as 'todo' temporarily).\n\nIn `@src/common/types/CardInfoType.ts`:\n- Around line 2-10: The cardNumbers field is declared too loosely as string[];\nchange it to a fixed 4-tuple (e.g. [string, string, string, string] or a branded\nalias) and update the setter signature in CardInfoHandlersType (setCardNumbers)\nto accept that same tuple type so callers like CardRegisterPage\n(useState(['','','',''])) and components relying on NumberField/INPUT_COUNT=4\nget compile-time safety; first scan call sites that pass arrays and adjust them\nto return/accept the 4-tuple type, then update the CardInfoType.cardNumbers and\nCardInfoHandlersType.setCardNumbers types accordingly.\n\nIn\n`@src/feature/CardRegister/components/CardPreviewSection/CardBrandLogo/CardBrandLogo.tsx`:\n- Around line 1-2: 현재 CardBrandLogo.tsx에서 visaImg와 masterCardImg를 깊은 상대경로로\nimport하고 있어 파일 이동 시 깨질 위험이 있습니다; CardBrandLogo.tsx의 import visaImg와 import\nmasterCardImg를 public 폴더의 루트 절대경로 방식으로 바꿔 (/images/Visa.png,\n/images/Mastercard.png 같이) 참조하도록 수정하고, 컴포넌트 내에서 해당 변수명(visaImg, masterCardImg)을\n그대로 사용하도록 유지하세요.\n\nIn\n`@src/feature/CardRegister/components/CardPreviewSection/CardPreviewSection.stories.tsx`:\n- Around line 23-31: Add a separate Storybook story for a MasterCard case in the\nsame file alongside the existing export const Filled: Story to enable\nbrand-specific visual regression checks; create a new export (e.g., export const\nMasterCard: Story) that mirrors Filled but sets cardInfo.cardNumbers to a\nMasterCard BIN prefix (e.g., starting with \"51\" or \"55\") and the same\nexpiryMonth/expiryYear fields so the preview renders the MasterCard logo/preview\nfor testing.\n\nIn `@src/feature/CardRegister/components/InfoInputSection/InfoInputSection.tsx`:\n- Around line 22-24: The render currently contains a console.log('error') inside\nthe InfoInputSection component that runs on every render when isError is true;\nremove this inline log or move it into a useEffect to avoid render-time side\neffects (e.g., add useEffect(() => { if (isError) { /* log */ } }, [isError]) ),\nreferencing the isError check in InfoInputSection to locate and replace the\nconsole.log.\n\nIn `@src/styles/reset.css`:\n- Around line 11-24: The reset.css currently mixes layout responsibilities into\nglobal selectors (html, body, `#root`) by setting height:100vh and centering via\nflexbox; remove the viewport-height and centering rules from these selectors so\nthe reset only contains neutral defaults, and move layout/centering styles into\nthe page-level wrapper (e.g., CardRegisterPage wrapper component or the App root\ncontainer) by applying the flexbox centering and min-height/height rules there\ninstead; update selectors referencing html, body, `#root` in reset.css to omit\ndisplay, justify-content, align-items, min-height and height so Storybook and\nother pages aren’t affected.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪄 Autofix (Beta)</summary>\n\nFix all unresolved CodeRabbit comments on this PR:\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"4b0d0e0a-96d7-4f10-b296-3a18ea78f0b9\"} --> Push a commit to this branch (recommended)\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"ff5b1114-7d8c-49e6-8ac1-43f82af23a33\"} --> Create a new PR with the fixes\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: Organization UI\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n**Run ID**: `2e52b9bc-157e-4823-a572-0bab1296c579`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 8d4c2c73f7cce87ffaae55245ae1cfd10228981d and a796e35a60518b1a493acd6b4248a40a629ef81c.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters (8)</summary>\n\n* `dist/assets/index-BtE7FqGX.js` is excluded by `!**/dist/**`\n* `dist/assets/index-CSiKPAGm.css` is excluded by `!**/dist/**`\n* `dist/images/Mastercard.png` is excluded by `!**/dist/**`, `!**/*.png`\n* `dist/images/Visa.png` is excluded by `!**/dist/**`, `!**/*.png`\n* `dist/index.html` is excluded by `!**/dist/**`\n* `package-lock.json` is excluded by `!**/package-lock.json`\n* `public/images/Mastercard.png` is excluded by `!**/*.png`\n* `public/images/Visa.png` is excluded by `!**/*.png`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected 